    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0185" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg175"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/9–148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-10-01T20:00:00-05:00">October 1, 1948—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1388. Response Chinese request Dept Sept 30 authorized Treasury pay direct to
                    Army approximately $38 million to provide arms and ammo chargeable against $125
                    million grants (Deptel 1338 Sept 18<anchor n="20" xml:id="d129-f1"/> ). Army has
                    indicated discussion re prices continuing with Chinese and availability checks
                    in progress to determine source from which stocks will come.</p>
                <p>Including this payment disbursements from grants as of Sept. 30 totaled
                    $88,275,409.62.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d129-f1" n="20" xml:id="d129-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it repeated text of memorandum by the Joint Chiefs of Staff,
                    September 9, <ref target="#pg167">p. 167</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
